5. Difference between INFO and DEBUG log levels

→ INFO records important application events, such as successful startup or business operations.
→ DEBUG provides detailed information for troubleshooting application behaviour.
→ Production normally uses INFO to reduce log volume.
→ DEBUG can be enabled temporarily when investigating an issue, while avoiding sensitive data.

