7. What are @Primary and @Qualifier?

→ @Primary marks the default bean when multiple beans of the same type exist.
→ @Qualifier selects a specific bean by its qualifier.
→ @Primary is useful for a default implementation.
→ @Qualifier is useful when I need a particular implementation.

Example:

@Service("emailService")
class EmailService implements NotificationService {}

@Service("smsService")
class SmsService implements NotificationService {}

@Autowired
@Qualifier("smsService")
private NotificationService notificationService;

