11. What is FeignClient?

→ FeignClient is a declarative HTTP client used to call another service.
→ I define an interface and annotate it with @FeignClient.
→ Spring creates the implementation and handles the HTTP request.
→ It reduces boilerplate code compared with manually building HTTP requests.

Example:

@FeignClient(name = "student-service")
public interface StudentClient {
    @GetMapping("/students/{id}")
    Student getStudent(@PathVariable Long id);
}

→ I configure timeouts, error handling, and retries where appropriate.

