12. How do you implement retry and timeout in WebClient?

→ A timeout prevents a request from waiting indefinitely.
→ Retry repeats a failed operation a limited number of times.
→ I use Reactor's timeout() and retryWhen() operators.
→ I retry only appropriate transient failures and avoid blindly retrying non-idempotent operations.

Example:

WebClient client = WebClient.builder()
    .baseUrl("http://student-service")
    .build();

Mono<String> response = client.get()
    .uri("/students/1")
    .retrieve()
    .bodyToMono(String.class)
    .timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(2))
    .retryWhen(
        Retry.backoff(3, Duration.ofMillis(200))
            .filter(ex -> ex instanceof TimeoutException)
    );

→ This example retries timeouts up to three times, with exponential backoff.
→ In production, I would also handle HTTP 5xx responses, connection failures, and total request deadlines carefully.

